WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.410
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Sunday, November 8.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.700
Sleep on it. This week, mice with some sleep cells silenced slept normally,

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.710
but forgot what they'd learned.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.560
And people who fell asleep earlier lost more weight, however long they slept.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.850
And Anthropic says its Claude agents dream too: between jobs,

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.840
they review past sessions to fix their notes.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.420
In China, a gene therapy plus a pill dimmed overactive brain cells,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.840
cutting seizures in three patients.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.350
Cambridge's AI-designed bird flu vaccine fully protected

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.950
mice and ferrets; the stockpiled one protected about half.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.840
And the NHS is trialling Dora,

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.000
an AI that phones people with fragile bones for routine check-ins.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.640
An old liver drug, UDCA, joins the world's biggest Parkinson's trial,

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.790
to see if it slows the disease.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.000
In mice, a Korean team's protein cut Alzheimer's plaques by about half,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.960
and helped one kind of memory.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.910
A review in Science says obesity drugs might protect thinking,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.930
if taken before damage sets in.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.540
And a Lancet trial found frail older people with f

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.590
ailing kidneys did about as well without dialysis.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.930
Here in Australia, Queensland researchers found exam stress in campus sewage,

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.360
as stress markers rose in exam weeks.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.530
In a thousand chats, the best had pink noise: stay on topic,

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.880
wander off, find each other again.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.180
Now, the catch. A working paper found AI improved lawyers' drafts,

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.900
but only seniors got sharper on their own.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.520
And in a survey,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.510
only younger psychedelic users reported less anxiety and depression; the link faded with age.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.810
Out in space,

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:08.590
an orbiter sniffed acid gas by a Martian volcano: Mars may still simmer inside.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.140
Meet Hopcopter: a drone that hops on one leg,

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:15.450
and its new foot handles sand, ice and rocks.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.180
And Sony's tiny desk screen shows 3D characters with no glasses,

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.160
landing in Japan in December.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.910
So, big decision this week? Sleep on it.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.360
Our brains do their best filing while we rest.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.140
Live long. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
